From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi: sun50i-di300: fix the UV order bit, limit
 semi-planar output

FMT_UVSEQ set means VU order (vendor DI_UVSEQ_VU for NV21/NV61), but
the driver set it for NV12/NV16. Same-format streams were unaffected;
on the H616 an NV12 source with a planar capture format came out with
Cb and Cr swapped, and NV16 to YUV422P wrote a broken Cr plane. Set the
bit for NV21/NV61, as the vendor does.

A planar source with a semi-planar capture format (YUV420 to NV12)
never completed: the engine stayed busy. Only allow a semi-planar
capture format that equals the source format.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c         | 28 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
index 4b8e58aef..73452155c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
@@ -100,11 +100,12 @@ static bool deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(u32 pixelformat)
 	}
 }
 
-static bool deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_first(u32 pixelformat)
+/* V before U in the combined chroma plane (FMT_UVSEQ set, as the vendor) */
+static bool deinterlace_fmt_is_vu(u32 pixelformat)
 {
 	switch (pixelformat) {
-	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
-	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV16:
+	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21:
+	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV61:
 		return true;
 	default:
 		return false;
@@ -478,11 +479,13 @@ static void deinterlace_device_run(void *priv)
 	reg = DEINTERLACE_FMT_IN0(f0_hw) | DEINTERLACE_FMT_IN1(f1_hw) |
 	      DEINTERLACE_FMT_IN2(src_hw) | DEINTERLACE_FMT_DIT(dst_hw) |
 	      DEINTERLACE_FMT_TNR(tnr_hw);
-	/* one UV order for all semi-planar buffers (try_fmt keeps them equal) */
-	if ((deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat) &&
-	     deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_first(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat)) ||
-	    (deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(ctx->dst_fmt.pixelformat) &&
-	     deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_first(ctx->dst_fmt.pixelformat)))
+	/*
+	 * One UV order for all semi-planar buffers (try_fmt keeps them
+	 * equal). UVSEQ set means VU order: with it set, NV12 input came out
+	 * of a planar capture format with Cb and Cr swapped.
+	 */
+	if (deinterlace_fmt_is_vu(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat) ||
+	    deinterlace_fmt_is_vu(ctx->dst_fmt.pixelformat))
 		reg |= DEINTERLACE_FMT_UVSEQ;
 	deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_FMT, reg);
 
@@ -1115,9 +1118,12 @@ static int deinterlace_try_fmt_vid_cap(struct file *file, void *priv,
 	    deinterlace_fmt_is_422(f->fmt.pix.pixelformat) !=
 	    deinterlace_fmt_is_422(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat))
 		f->fmt.pix.pixelformat = ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat;
-	/* one UV order bit covers every semi-planar buffer */
-	if (deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(f->fmt.pix.pixelformat) &&
-	    deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat))
+	/*
+	 * One UV order bit covers every semi-planar buffer. A semi-planar
+	 * output from a planar input never completed on the H616 (engine
+	 * busy forever), so a semi-planar output needs the same input.
+	 */
+	if (deinterlace_fmt_is_uv_combined(f->fmt.pix.pixelformat))
 		f->fmt.pix.pixelformat = ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat;
 	f->fmt.pix.field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 	f->fmt.pix.width = ctx->src_fmt.width;
-- 
2.55.0

